# Without this file, `COPY . .` in the Dockerfile copies the HOST node_modules
# straight over the one the `deps` stage just installed inside Alpine.
#
# That is not only slow -- it sends a few hundred MB to the daemon on every
# build and defeats the point of a separate deps layer -- it is wrong. This
# repository is developed on Windows, so the host tree carries
# `@next/swc-win32-x64-msvc` where the image needs `@next/swc-linux-x64-musl`.
# A native binary for the wrong platform is the kind of thing that either
# falls back silently to something slower or fails on a machine that is not
# the one it was built on.
node_modules
.next
out

# Local state and secrets have no business in a build context.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.log
npm-debug.log*

.git
.gitignore
.vscode
.idea
*.tsbuildinfo

# Tests and docs do not ship in the standalone output.
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.tsx
vitest.config.mts
vitest.setup.ts
README.md
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md
